The city clerk may decline to consider an application for a city license under this chapter on any of the following grounds:
(1) Failure of the applicant to meet state requirements for state license;
(2) Failure of the applicant to pay required fees and taxes;
(3) Failure of the applicant to provide required valid information, documents and the like;
(4) False information in the application or attached documents;
(5) Failure of the applicant to pass review by the chief of police;
(6) Improper residency of the applicant, owner or registered agent;
(7) Prior convictions of the applicant as provided in this chapter; or
(8) Failure to meet any other requirements in this chapter for a license of the class applied for.
(Code 1992, § 3-39; Ord. No. 2007-11, 12-4-2007; Ord. No. 2013-10, 12-3-2013)

